# Required elements: Roman domus (villa urbana), "villa-sonnet"

Frame: site x 0..35, z 0..47, y 0..9 (ridges <= y9, one chimney may reach y10). Front = NORTH (-z); street is at z<0.
Ground y=0, street sidewalk z=0..1. House footprint x 0..35, z 2..45 stands on a podium: foundation y=0, FLOOR y=1, so a player
inside stands at y=2 (air y2..5, wall top / ceiling y=6, roofs y7..9). Outdoors on the sidewalk a player stands at y=1.
Mirror rule: the house is symmetric about the axis between x=17 and x=18: x' = 35 - x. Vocabulary names are in plan.md.
"Part" = plan.md part number (P1 shell, P2 roofs, P3 street, P4 atrium, P5 peristyle, P6 finish). "Room designer" = the room's own interior designer.

| # | Element | Real construction, block by block | Coordinates | Part | Vocab |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| E1 | Symmetrical street front | Wall z=2, x=0..35: y1 `stone_bricks` plinth; y2..3 `red_terracotta` dado; y4..5 cream plaster; y6 `cut_sandstone` cornice course. Openings: fauces centre, 4 shop windows (3..5, 10..13, 22..25, 30..32) mirror pairs. Quartz pilasters frame the fauces. | x0..35, y1..6, z2 | P1 (wall, openings), P3 (doors, counters, shutters) | wallCell, pilaster, shopWindow |
| E2 | Recessed entrance (fauces) | Corridor 4 wide: front wall z=2 is OMITTED at x16..19 (y2..5) so the forecourt z2..3 is open to the street; doors set back at z=4; side walls x=15 and x=20 (z3..8); lintel beam y6 `smooth_quartz` at z=2 x15..20; pilasters at (15,z2) and (20,z2). Corridor runs z=2..9 and opens into the atrium through the z=9 wall (x16..19, y2..5). | x16..19, y2..5, z2..9 | P1 shell, P3 doors | pilaster, doorPair |
| E3 | Fauces doors | Two double doors of `spruce_door` (4 doors in a row, hinge pairs 16+17 and 18+19, `half` lower+upper, `open=true` so a player can walk in, `facing=north`) at z=4. Above them at z=4: y4 fanlight row of `spruce_trapdoor` (half=top, open=false), y5 lintel row `dark_oak_planks`. | x16..19, y2..5 at z=4 | P3 | doorPair |
| E4 | Entrance step | `stone_brick_stairs` facing=south, half=bottom at (16..19, y1, z1) (step from sidewalk y0 to floor y1); the floor (y1) starts at z=2. | x16..19, y1, z1 | P3 | step |
| E5 | Four shop rooms (tabernae) | Box rooms 6 deep. Street window each with a masonry counter: `stone_brick_slab` type=bottom on the whole opening at y2, one `decorated_pot` on the counter at the opening's second cell (y3), `barrel` pair inside the shop behind the counter. Windows: W1 x3..5, W2 x10..13, E3 x22..25, E4 x30..32, y2..4 (3 tall), lintel y5. | see plan ROOMS/OPENINGS | P1 openings, P3 counters | shopWindow |
| E6 | Shop shutters | Open `spruce_trapdoor` panels (open=true, facing=north, half=bottom) lying flat on the wall face in the sidewalk cells z=1, one stack of 2 (y3,y4) on each side of each shop window: x2,6 / 9,14 / 21,26 / 29,33. | z1, y3..4 | P3 | shutter |
| E7 | Atrium open to the sky (compluvium) | Rectangular opening in the ceiling AND roof: x14..21, z13..18 (8x6). Ceiling (y6) stops at the opening; edge beams y6 `dark_oak_log` around its perimeter (axis x on z=13 and z=18, axis z on x=14 and x=21). Four inward-sloping roof strips (pinwheel) leave the hole clear. | x14..21, y6..9, z13..18 | P1 (ceiling hole), P2 (roof hole), P4 (beams) | beam |
| E8 | Shallow rain pool (impluvium) | Basin 6x4 x15..20, z14..17: y0 `blue_terracotta` (lining), y1 `water` source blocks (flush with floor). Raised coping ring around it: `smooth_quartz_slab` type=bottom at y2 on the 20 perimeter cells of x14..21,z13..18 minus the 4 corner columns. Every water cell is fenced by floor blocks on all 4 sides and floor below: no leak. | x14..21, y0..2, z13..18 | P1 (y0 lining, y1 ring left as floor), P4 (water, coping) | impluvium |
| E9 | Atrium columns | 4 Tuscan columns at the corners of the compluvium (14,13),(21,13),(14,18),(21,18): y2 `stone_bricks` base, y3..4 `dark_oak_log` axis=y, y5 `dark_oak_planks` capital; they carry the edge beams (E7). | x14|21, y2..5, z13|18 | P4 | tuscanColumn |
| E10 | Tablinum (study) | Room x11..24, z23..30 on the axis facing the fauces. Both ends open: north to the atrium (x15..20, y2..5, in z=22), south to the peristyle (x15..20, y2..5, in z=31), so the whole axis fauces-atrium-tablinum-garden is visible. Pilaster pair framing each opening: `quartz_pillar` at x14 and x21 (y2..5). Furniture (desk of `lectern`+`bookshelf`, scroll shelves, chair) by room designer. | x11..24, y2..5, z23..30 | P1, P4 (pilasters, arch), designer | pilaster |
| E11 | Peristyle garden court | Open-sky garden x11..24, z35..41 (14x7), ground layer y1: `grass_block` lawn, `gravel` path ring, parterre beds, fountain, statues. Ringed on all four sides by the colonnade (E12). | x11..24, y1..2, z35..41 | P5 | gardenBed |
| E12 | Covered colonnade of white columns | Column line = rectangle x10..25, z34..42. Columns at x in {10,13,16,19,22,25} on z=34 and z=42, and at z in {34,36,38,40,42} on x=10 and x=25 (corners shared) = 6+6+3+3 = 18 columns. Column: y2 `quartz_block` base, y3..4 `quartz_pillar` axis=y, y5 `chiseled_quartz_block` capital. Continuous architrave y6 `smooth_quartz` along the whole column rectangle. Stylobate under the line y1 `smooth_stone`. Ring walkway (covered) x7..28, z32..44 outside the court. | x7..28, y1..6, z32..44 | P5 (columns, architrave, floor edge), P1 (walkway floor + ceiling) | column |
| E13 | Formal planting | Two symmetric parterre beds 3x5: W x12..14, z36..40; E x21..23, z36..40. Border = hedge (E14); inside cells (13,y2,37),(13,y2,39) and (22,y2,37),(22,y2,39): flowers `poppy`/`azure_bluet` on `grass_block` y1; (13|22, z38) a statue (E16). Plus `rose_bush` at (11,2,35),(24,2,35) and `lilac` at (11,2,41),(24,2,41) (ring-path corners, on `grass_block`). | see plan | P5 | gardenBed |
| E14 | Low hedges | Hedge = `azalea_leaves` (persistent) 1 high at y2, placed on the border cells of each bed (12 cells per bed), with a `flowering_azalea_leaves` every 4th cell. | x12..14|21..23, y2, z36..40 | P5 | hedge |
| E15 | Fountain | Basin rim x15..20, z36..40 perimeter: `smooth_quartz` full blocks at y2 (rim, holds the water); basin floor y1 `blue_terracotta` for interior x16..19, z37..39; `water` at y2 on the interior cells except the pedestal; central pedestal (17..18, z38): `quartz_pillar` y2..3 and `water_cauldron` (level 3) on top at y4 on each of the two pedestal columns. Water cells = the 12 interior cells minus the 2 pedestal cells = 10. | x15..20, y1..4, z36..40 | P5 | fountain |
| E16 | Statues | Statue = plinth + figure, white: `stone_bricks` y2, `diorite_wall` y3 (robe), `quartz_pillar` y4 (torso), `skeleton_skull` y5 (head, rotation to face the axis). Four statues: (13,38),(22,38) in the beds, and (8,33) and (27,33) at the walkway corners; plus 2 in atrium niches (11,12) and (24,12) placed by P4. | listed | P4, P5 | statue |
| E17 | Triclinium (dining room, couches on three sides) | Room x26..34, z23..30. Three couches (klinai) on the W, N and E sides, open to the south doorway; low table in the middle. Couch = 2 `red_bed` pieces end to end against the wall + `dark_oak_slab` side rails. Table = `dark_oak_fence` post + `dark_oak_slab`. Mosaic floor, wall niche with a lamp. | x26..34, y2..5, z23..30 | P1 shell, designer | couch |
| E18 | Cubicula (small bedrooms) x6 | Six small rooms (C1,C2 W and C3,C4 E off the atrium; C5, C7 off the peristyle). Each: `white_bed` or `red_bed`, `chest`, small lamp, door to court. Interior designer's choice. | see ROOMS | P1, designers | bed |
| E19 | Kitchen (culina) with hearth | Room x1..9, z23..30. Hearth against the west wall: pad (1..3, y2, 25..27) `stone_bricks`; `campfire` (lit=true) at (2,y3,26); hood y5 ring of `stone_brick_stairs` around (2,5,26); ceiling hole (2,6,26) and a hollow stack above it (E31). Counter: `smoker`, `furnace`, `crafting_table`, `barrel`s, `water_cauldron`. | x1..9, y2..5, z23..30 | P1, P2 (stack), designer | hearth |
| E20 | Terracotta tile roofs sloping inward to the courts | Sheds with the LOW edge at the court: atrium strips fall to the compluvium, peristyle strips fall to the column line; wing gables on the side rooms; front block gable ridge along x (visible tile from the street). All in `red-tile` (brick/granite mix, `mud_brick` eave). | y7..9 | P2 | roofPiece |
| E21 | Cream plaster walls | Walls y4..5 hashed `smooth_sandstone` 70 / `end_stone_bricks` 20 / `sandstone` 10, inside and out. | all walls | P1 | wallCell |
| E22 | Red painted dado | y2..3 `red_terracotta`, inside and out, on every wall (not on the columns). | all walls | P1 | wallCell |
| E23 | Mosaic floors | Floor y1, laid by P1 per room (table in plan PALETTE/ROOMS): atrium black/white checker with red border; tablinum bordered panel with a central emblem; triclinium meander border + central emblem; cubicula plain with a border. | y1 | P1 | mosaic |
| E24 | Bronze lamps | `copper_lantern` hanging (hanging=true) from `copper_chain` under the ceiling at y4 (chain y5), 12 hanging lamps; standing lampstands (`cut_copper_slab` bottom y2, `copper_bars` y3, `copper_lantern` y4) beside the fauces, the tablinum opening, and the doors of the triclinium and the rear. | plan lists | P6 | hangLamp, lampStand |
| E25 | Potted plants | `potted_*` blocks (fern, azalea bush, flowering azalea bush, cornflower, allium) on `stone_brick_slab` pedestals y2 (pot at y3), in the fauces, atrium corners, walkways and the street front. | plan lists | P6 | pot |
| E26 | Rear service door (posticum) | 2 wide opening (17..18, y2..3, z45) in the back wall with `spruce_door` pair; rear lane z46..47 of `gravel`/`dirt_path`. | x17..18, z45..47 | P1, P6 | doorPair |
| E27 | Lararium (house shrine) | Room C6 x1..5, z39..44: niche shrine at the west wall: `stone_brick_stairs`/`quartz_slab` altar, `candle`s, `copper_lantern`, two `potted_*`. Designer places. | x1..5, z39..44 | P1, designer | pot |
| E28 | Barred windows | Small windows 1 wide, y3..4: `copper_bars` filling the opening, listed in OPENINGS; they line up with the rooms behind them. | OPENINGS | P1 leaves, P3/P6 fill | windowGrille |
| E29 | Pavement and kerb (street) | Sidewalk z0..1, y0: `andesite` 60 / `polished_andesite` 40 hashed; kerb: `stone_brick_slab` type=bottom at y1, z=0, x0..35. | x0..35, z0..1 | P3 | pavement |
| E30 | Cornice and entrance pediment | Cornice course y6 `cut_sandstone` all around; above the fauces a three-step triangular pediment of `quartz_stairs` / `smooth_quartz` at y7..9, x14..21, z=2 (built by the roof tool's `pediment` option or P2 by hand). | x14..21, y7..9, z2..3 | P2 | pediment |
| E31 | Kitchen chimney stack | Hollow 3x3 stack `stone_bricks` x1..3, z25..27, y6..9, hollow core (2, y6..9, 26), campfire smoke exits at the top. Top may reach y10. | x1..3, y6..9, z25..27 | P2 | chimney |
